#!/bin/bash
# TN column truth loop — self-paced; new session: /loop $(tail -1 TN_COLS_LOOP.sh)
# Roadmap: docs/TN_COLUMN_AUDIT_ROADMAP.md (doctrine §0, anchors §1, constraints §2, measured state §3, ledger §4)
# Instrument: cd apps/market-ui && npx playwright test tnColumnAudit --config=playwright.config.ts

Read docs/TN_COLUMN_AUDIT_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard constraints exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 4; that task's Accept line is the acceptance test, and nothing else in Section 4 may be touched in the same pass. TRUTH: never invent a number, a threshold, or an API behaviour to make a column look filled — read the actual anchors first (MarketList.tsx column defs + cellFor, api/tn/[fn].ts board/fundamentals/engine/intraday, marketsHub.ts row mapping) and re-measure against prod rather than trusting Section 3, which is a dated snapshot; if a measurement disagrees with Section 3, the fresh measurement wins and you correct Section 3 in the same commit. A cell with no supporting datum renders an em dash — filling it with a neutral default, a carried-forward value, or a plausible-looking estimate is the exact defect this loop exists to remove, so a task is never "done" by making the audit numbers prettier. Absence of data is a legitimate answer: a stock that did not trade has no volume and no day range, and that must survive the fix. Respect the blob cache: /api/tn/* is cached 120-180s with stale-while-revalidate, so after deploying re-read the endpoint until the blob rolls before believing any number, and never conclude from a single call. Reuse existing plumbing: the cached() helper, the lazy per-group fetch pattern in MarketList, the fmtPrice/fmtPct null-tolerant formatters; no new npm deps (check package.json), no new endpoints where an existing one can carry the field. A task is done only when: its Accept line is demonstrably satisfied by a real run, npx tsc -b is clean from apps/market-ui, npx vitest run shows no new failures, npx playwright test tnColumnAudit tnNullFeed passes (tnNullFeed must never regress - the TN route has been blanked three times by formatters assuming a number), and vercel --prod from repo root ran if UI or api changed. Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 5 progress-log row with REAL numbers from that run (fill counts, distinct counts, mismatch counts - no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "fix(tn-cols): TNC-n <what> - <verify numbers>" (use git commit -F file, apostrophes in a -m string break the shell). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on a usage or rate limit or 429 or overload - stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger plus progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step; log partial progress BEFORE long or risky operations. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 4, or a task blocked on user-only input such as credentials or a dead upstream feed - then say exactly what is needed, note it in the ledger, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining tasks are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
